{"name":"Oil Rush","hex":"#333144","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Liquid fat.","Petroleum-based liquid used as fuel or lubricant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lubricate with oil.","To grease with oil for cooking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oil"},{"term":"rush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sudden forward motion.","A surge, a sudden increase."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hurry; to perform a task with great haste, often not properly or without thinking carefully.","To flow or move forward rapidly or noisily."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oil Rush","blocks":[{"text":"Oil Rush is a tower defense real-time strategy game developed by UNIGINE Holding S.à r.l. using their Unigine engine technology. Set in a flooded, post-apocalyptic world, the game consists of players fighting over control of the world's last remaining oil reserves. The game was released as a digital download for Microsoft Windows, Linux, and OS X."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4e/Oil_Rush_cover.png/330px-Oil_Rush_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil_Rush","wikidata":"Q4045698"},{"title":"Oil","blocks":[{"text":"Oil is a liquid with varying degrees of viscosity depending on temperature. Oil is any nonpolar chemical substance that is composed primarily of hydrocarbons and is hydrophobic and lipophilic. Oils are usually flammable and surface active. Most oils are unsaturated lipids that are liquid at room temperature."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil","wikidata":"Q42962"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Italian_olive_oil_2007.jpg/500px-Italian_olive_oil_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wi